{"name":"Dowager","hex":"#838c82","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dowager","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A widow holding property or title derived from her late husband.","The widow of the holder of a title (usually a member of the peerage or a baronet); used in combination with the title she held during her husband's lifetime."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dowager"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dowager","blocks":[{"text":"A dowager is a widow who holds a title or property – a \"dower\" – derived from her deceased spouse. As an adjective, dowager usually appears in association with monarchical and aristocratic titles. There is no male equivalent as men keep all properties and titles outright, not needing to relinquish any titles or positions for the next in line, with exception to Prince Consort which would be removed, as consort denotes a spouse of a monarch."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dowager"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Louis_XIV_of_France_and_his_family_attributed_to_Nicolas_de_Largilli%C3%A8re.jpg/500px-Louis_XIV_of_France_and_his_family_attributed_to_Nicolas_de_Largilli%C3%A8re.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Louis_XIV_of_France_and_his_family_attributed_to_Nicolas_de_Largilli%C3%A8re.jpg/500px-Louis_XIV_of_France_and_his_family_attributed_to_Nicolas_de_Largilli%C3%A8re.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Dowager Duchess of Ventadour in full mourning attends the King of France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALouis_XIV_of_France_and_his_family_attributed_to_Nicolas_de_Largilli%C3%A8re.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/L%27imp%C3%A9ratrice_Eug%C3%A9nie_en_deuil_1873.jpg/500px-L%27imp%C3%A9ratrice_Eug%C3%A9nie_en_deuil_1873.jpg?utm_sou